-- title:
--   Nonzero congruence ideal for a reduced augmented algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain, and let $T$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure such that $T$ is finite as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, $T$ is a Noetherian ring, and $T$ is reduced. Let $\pi_T \colon T \to \mathcal{O}$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras. Write $\mathfrak{p} = \ker \pi_T$ for its kernel, an ideal of $T$, and let $\operatorname{Ann}_T(\mathfrak{p})$ be the annihilator of that ideal, i.e. the ideal of elements $t \in T$ with $t x = 0$ for all $x \in \mathfrak{p}$. The assertion is that the ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ generated by the image $\pi_T(\operatorname{Ann}_T(\mathfrak{p}))$ — the congruence ideal $\eta_T$ of the augmentation $\pi_T$ — is not the zero ideal; equivalently, some element annihilating $\ker \pi_T$ has nonzero image under $\pi_T$.
--
--   This is the standing nondegeneracy hypothesis $\eta_T \neq (0)$ of the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion for complete intersections, discharged once and for all for reduced Noetherian algebras that are module-finite over a domain. It is used in the construction and verification of patching data and in the applications of the numerical criterion to local Hecke algebras, where reducedness of the Hecke algebra is available.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgHom_congruenceIdeal_ne_bot_of_isReduced.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Maps
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Nilpotent.Defs
